SUMMARY:Fjord
LOCATION:West Newton Cinema\, 1296 Washington St\, Newton\, MA 02465
DESCRIPTION:Mihai and Lisbet Gheorghiu\, a Romanian-Norwegian Pentecostal c
 ouple\, move with their five children from Romania to Norway after Mihai
 ’s parents die\, seeking closeness to Lisbet’s family\, who share thei
 r faith. Settling in an isolated coastal village\, they form a bond with t
 heir neighbors\, the Halbergs. When their daughter Elia appears at school 
 with bruises\, suspicions arise about the family's strict religious upbrin
 ging. Fjord explores clashing worldviews\, conformity\, tolerance\, and th
 e boundaries of freedom and intimacy.\nhttps://www.westnewtoncinema.com/mo
 vie/fjord\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.westnewtoncinema.com/movie/fjord
